<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-25T14:09:15+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:09:15 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[In 2014, scientists set off 23 blasts to uncover magma hidden beneath Mount St Helens]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133500774.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking study, researchers utilized controlled explosions paired with seismic technology to investigate Mount St. Helens' subterranean magma systems. They discovered a magma-reservoir located between four to fifteen kilometers deep. This extensive analysis employed numerous instruments to track seismic waves within the volcano, yielding vital knowledge about magma movements. Such understanding is instrumental in forecasting volcanic activity and potential eruptions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2014-scientists-set-off-23-explosions-and-deployed-3500-seismographs-around-mount-st-helens-the-experiment-helped-image-a-magma-reservoir-roughly-4-to-15-km-beneath-the-volcano/articleshow/133500774.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2014-scientists-set-off-23-explosions-and-deployed-3500-seismographs-around-mount-st-helens-the-experiment-helped-image-a-magma-reservoir-roughly-4-to-15-km-beneath-the-volcano/articleshow/133500774.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T13:55:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133501316,imgsize-1160873.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists reidentify Ireland’s “Kerry Cow” bones as bear and wild boar, challenging farming theory]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133497087.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ancient animal bones from Ferriters Cove are now identified as bear and wild boar. This reclassification challenges decades of evidence for early farming in Ireland. Previously thought to be cattle, these remains are now understood differently. Modern scientific techniques revealed the true identity of these ancient specimens. This discovery prompts a reconsideration of Ireland's prehistoric transition to agriculture.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-reidentify-irelands-famous-kerry-cow-bones-as-ancient-bear-and-wild-boar-remains-challenging-a-long-held-theory-about-how-farming-reached-the-island/articleshow/133497087.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-reidentify-irelands-famous-kerry-cow-bones-as-ancient-bear-and-wild-boar-remains-challenging-a-long-held-theory-about-how-farming-reached-the-island/articleshow/133497087.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T13:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133497493,imgsize-1036722.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wallabies came to New Zealand in 1912; they now threaten to spread across a third of the country]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133497371.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wallabies introduced to New Zealand more than a century ago have now spread across more than 200,000 hectares in the Bay of Plenty region. The animals feed on native tree seedlings, ferns and grasses, damage plantation trees and compete with livestock for pasture. Authorities warn that unchecked wallabies could eventually occupy one-third of New Zealand by 2065 and cause $84 million in annual damage.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1912-new-zealand-released-wallabies-near-rotorua-they-now-occupy-more-than-200000-hectares-and-if-left-unchecked-could-spread-across-a-third-of-the-country-by-2065-causing-84-million-in-damage-a-year/articleshow/133497371.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-1912-new-zealand-released-wallabies-near-rotorua-they-now-occupy-more-than-200000-hectares-and-if-left-unchecked-could-spread-across-a-third-of-the-country-by-2065-causing-84-million-in-damage-a-year/articleshow/133497371.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T13:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133499184,imgsize-171770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Jeremiah Bents, the Minnesota student who recreated Mars soil to test water cleanup]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133495002.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jeremiah Bents, a Minnesota student, explored water filtration using Mars soil simulant. His project examined ammonia removal from contaminated water in a laboratory setting. This innovative work earned him the Earth Systems Science Award at a state science fair. He received guidance from university researchers and a NASA scientist. Bents' experiment demonstrated a practical application for future space missions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-jeremiah-bents-the-minnesota-student-who-recreated-mars-soil-in-a-lab-to-test-whether-future-astronauts-could-clean-contaminated-water/articleshow/133495002.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-jeremiah-bents-the-minnesota-student-who-recreated-mars-soil-in-a-lab-to-test-whether-future-astronauts-could-clean-contaminated-water/articleshow/133495002.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133495307,imgsize-1239939.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dr DisRespect vs Nickmercs controversy: Streamer threatens to assault Nickmercs in COD stream]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133498666.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dr DisRespect has seemingly threatened Nickmercs during aCall of Duty Modern Warfare 4Beta livestream. After a viewer asked about streamer skins, the Doc questioned whether Nickmercs was in the game before calling him a “phony” and “wannabe tough guy.” He also made a gesture suggesting a strike to the face. In another clip, Dr DisRespect claimed Nickmercs walked away after being confronted by him previously.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/dr-disrespect-vs-nickmercs-controversy-streamer-threatens-to-assault-nickmercs-during-call-of-duty-stream/articleshow/133498666.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/dr-disrespect-vs-nickmercs-controversy-streamer-threatens-to-assault-nickmercs-during-call-of-duty-stream/articleshow/133498666.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T12:55:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133499175,imgsize-143614.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nathan Cofnas on Jason Arday controversy: “This was about DEI”]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133497057.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-says-he-had-no-ill-will-towards-him-this-was-about-dei/articleshow/133497057.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-scholar-who-exposed-jason-ardays-plagiarism-says-he-had-no-ill-will-towards-him-this-was-about-dei/articleshow/133497057.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T12:28:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133498040,imgsize-2000090.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1984, Nasa sent thousands of honeybees into orbit to build honeycomb without gravity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133455600.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1984-nasa-sent-thousands-of-honeybees-into-space-to-build-a-honeycomb-without-gravity-and-the-tiny-colony-eventually-created-31-square-inches-of-comb/articleshow/133455600.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1984-nasa-sent-thousands-of-honeybees-into-space-to-build-a-honeycomb-without-gravity-and-the-tiny-colony-eventually-created-31-square-inches-of-comb/articleshow/133455600.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T16:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133455920,imgsize-164158.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists turn plastic waste into protein cookies; food can tackle hunger and feed space crews]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133452916.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers at Southern Illinois University Carbondale are developing protein-rich cookies made using plastic waste and agricultural waste. Called µBites, the cookies use PET plastic from bottles and discarded corn stalks and leaves. Programmed yeasts convert processed waste into proteins, fats, acids and flavouring molecules. The NASA-linked project is aimed at developing food for resource-limited environments, including future deep-space missions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-turned-plastic-bottles-and-corn-waste-into-protein-rich-cookies-the-food-could-help-tackle-hunger-problem-and-also-feed-space-crews/articleshow/133452916.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-turned-plastic-bottles-and-corn-waste-into-protein-rich-cookies-the-food-could-help-tackle-hunger-problem-and-also-feed-space-crews/articleshow/133452916.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T12:00:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133497076,imgsize-92171.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[“I deceived people, I lied”: Woman pretended to be a child for years, convicted of fraud]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133496640.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a shocking case from Brazil, Amanda Maria Souza de Oliveira was found guilty of fraud and assuming a false identity, having lived undetected as a child for years. Although she confessed to her masquerade, she maintained that her motivations were rooted in personal vulnerability rather than dishonesty. The court, however, sentenced her to prison for her deceptive actions, highlighting the seriousness of her offenses.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-deceived-people-i-lied-a-37-year-old-woman-pretrended-to-be-a-child-for-years-and-convinced-families-she-needed-protection-now-she-is-convicted-of-fraud/articleshow/133496640.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/i-deceived-people-i-lied-a-37-year-old-woman-pretrended-to-be-a-child-for-years-and-convinced-families-she-needed-protection-now-she-is-convicted-of-fraud/articleshow/133496640.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:57:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133496997,imgsize-382165.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[10-year-old found mystery spider; scientists later named new species after him]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133496233.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2020-10-year-old-murphy-widdowson-collected-a-spider-on-a-remote-australian-island-that-experts-could-not-identify-scientists-later-declared-it-a-new-species-and-named-it-artoriopsis-murphyi-after-him/articleshow/133496233.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2020-10-year-old-murphy-widdowson-collected-a-spider-on-a-remote-australian-island-that-experts-could-not-identify-scientists-later-declared-it-a-new-species-and-named-it-artoriopsis-murphyi-after-him/articleshow/133496233.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:40:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133496304,imgsize-93782.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1964, NASA bounced a laser off a satellite; today, it helps track melting ice]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133494356.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1926-a-10-ft-rocket-flew-41-ft-35-years-later-nasa-honored-its-creator-in-space/articleshow/133494356.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1926-a-10-ft-rocket-flew-41-ft-35-years-later-nasa-honored-its-creator-in-space/articleshow/133494356.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T13:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133495104,imgsize-82804.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mojtaba Khamenei seen, heard in rare video amid health concerns]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133494668.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/mojtaba-khamenei-seen-heard-in-rare-video-amid-health-concerns/articleshow/133494668.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/mojtaba-khamenei-seen-heard-in-rare-video-amid-health-concerns/articleshow/133494668.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:06:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133494804,imgsize-1001187.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Dr. Robert Parry: Ohio pediatric surgeon draws cartoons on kids’ bandages after surgery]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133494021.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dr-robert-parry-ohio-pediatric-surgeon-draws-cartoons-on-kids-bandages-after-surgery-creating-10000-moments-of-joy/articleshow/133494021.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-dr-robert-parry-ohio-pediatric-surgeon-draws-cartoons-on-kids-bandages-after-surgery-creating-10000-moments-of-joy/articleshow/133494021.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-25T11:03:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133494649,imgsize-1428158.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17-year-old Leon Wang finds 2 FDA-approved drugs that reduced Alzheimer’s-linked cell damage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133493022.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A young student's research explored existing medicines for Alzheimer's disease protection.  He identified two drugs, nintedanib and pirfenidone, showing protective effects in cell models.  This drug repurposing approach offers a faster, less expensive research starting point.  Wang's work hi